tion Studio and offers natural light, armchairs, puzzles, crafts, and leisure-reading books.","source_url":"https://library.sfsu.edu/news/faculty-fall-2025","source_title":"Centering students’ needs in reimagined spaces","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Located in LIB 124C, attached to the first-floor Collaboration Studio.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-library-silent-study-room","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Silent Study Room","title":"Silent Study Room","subtitle":"J. Paul Leonard Library, LIB 41","notes":"Choose this ground-floor room for distraction-light reading or writing; plan to keep conversation, food, phones, and audio outside the room.","short_summary":"A designated silent library room for heads-down individual work.","evidence_claim":"The Silent Study Room is on the library ground floor, and talking, eating, phone use, and audio devices are not allowed there.","source_url":"https://library.sfsu.edu/news/faculty-fall-2025","source_title":"Centering students’ needs in reimagined spaces","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Ground floor; the library floor map identifies it as LIB 41.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-digital-media-studio-makerspace","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Digital Media Studio and MakerSpace","title":"Digital Media Studio and MakerSpace","subtitle":"J. Paul Leonard Library, LIB 260","notes":"Use this second-floor studio when a class project needs 3D printing, VR, high-end computers, specialized software, scanning, or equipment checkout.","short_summary":"A hands-on media-production space with digital tools and equipment support.","evidence_claim":"The Dig