ary sources; contact Special Collections first if you need help preparing a request.","short_summary":"A fourth-floor reading room for working with rare books and primary-source material.","evidence_claim":"SFSU directs students seeking rare books and primary-source material to the Special Collections & Archives Reading Room on the library’s fourth floor.","source_url":"https://library.sfsu.edu/students","source_title":"Information for Students | J. Paul Leonard Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Fourth-floor LIB 460; contact Special Collections & Archives for research assistance or access questions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-library-quiet-study","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Quiet Study","title":"Quiet Study","subtitle":"J. Paul Leonard Library, LIB 485","notes":"Head to the fourth floor when you need a calmer reading or drafting block, and keep voices low so the shared quiet-study setting remains usable.","short_summary":"A designated fourth-floor quiet-study area among the library’s open stacks.","evidence_claim":"The library’s fourth floor is a quiet study area, and its floor map identifies Quiet Study in LIB 485.","source_url":"https://library.sfsu.edu/floor-maps","source_title":"Floor Maps | J. Paul Leonard Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Fourth floor; designated quiet areas require low voices and minimal talking.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-garden-of-remembrance","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Garden of Remembrance","title":"Garden of Remembrance","subtitle":"Between Burk Hall and the Fine Arts Building","notes":"Use the garden as a reflective pause on the way across campus, and read its memorial elements with attention to the history they commemorate.","short_summary":"A campus memorial garden honoring Japanese American incarceration and affected SF State students.","evidence_claim":"The Garden of Remembrance honors Japanese Americans incarcerated during World War II, including 19 SF State students, and is free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://gallery.sfsu.edu/visit-the-garden","source_title":"Visit the Garden | Fine Arts Gallery","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Located between Burk Hall and the Fine Arts Building; east and west entrances are described by the gallery.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-associated-students-art-gallery","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Associated Students Art Gallery","title":"Associated Students Art Gallery","subtitle":"Cesar Chavez Student Center, T-139","notes":"Check the exhibition schedule before visiting, then use a current show or reception as a starting point for conversation about artists and community issues.","short_summary":"A student-funded, student-staffed gallery presenting visual and interdisciplinary work.","evidence_claim":"Associated Students describes its Art Gallery as student-funded and student-staffed; it presents student, faculty, and professional work and hosts exhibits and events.","source_url":"https://asi.sfsu.edu/art-gallery","source_title":"Art Gallery | Associated Students","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"Located in the Student Center at T-139; consult the gallery’s current exhibition information before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sfsu-events-room","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Events Room","title":"Events Room","subtitle":"J. Paul Leonard Library, LIB 121","notes":"Look at the library events calendar before crossing the quad; use a listed workshop, talk, or program as an easy way to connect coursework with campus life.","short_summary":"A first-floor library venue used for campus workshops, talks, and other programs.","evidence_claim":"The library identifies the Events Room as LIB 121 on the first floor and lists it as a frequent location for events and meetings.","source_url":"https://library.sfsu.edu/spaces","source_title":"Spaces | J. Paul Leonard Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://maps.sfsu.edu/","access_notes":"LIB 121 on the first floor; availability changes when it is scheduled for events or meetings.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
